-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Aug 12 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>

- Fix s390x build: construct libc::sigaction from a zeroed value instead
  of struct-literal syntax. On s390x libc::sigaction carries a private
  __glibc_reserved0 field, so the upstream struct literal in
  proxmox-sys timer.rs failed to compile ("cannot construct sigaction
  with struct literal syntax due to private fields"). The zeroed
  construction assigns only public fields and is behaviour-identical on
  every architecture.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Aug 11 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>

- Add s390x architecture support (Debian s390x; RPM s390x). s390x is
  big-endian; the on-disk/on-wire pxar and datastore formats are
  little-endian by design (Endian-derive + le-value readers), so backups
  are cross-architecture compatible. Add the s390x pbs-buildcfg multiarch
  mapping.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Aug 11 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>

- Add Debian package architecture support for armhf and ppc64el.
- Patch bundled upstream sources for 32-bit libc::time_t, ARM32
  libc field widths including fuse-loop and pbs-client pxar
  create/extract/metadata stat/offset conversions, and ppc64le
  pbs-buildcfg multiarch detection.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Aug 08 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>

- Initial community/unofficial packaging of the Proxmox Backup client
  suite (proxmox-backup-client, pxar, proxmox-file-restore) built from
  upstream Rust sources at tag v4.2.0.
- File-level restore only; the VM/block-image restore path
  (proxmox-restore-daemon + prebuilt restore image) is out of scope.
